    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189#discussion_r3844186956\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note: This change to the benchmark was required to bench component calls with <code>concurrency_support</code> disabled. The previous setup would only run them with it enabled.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618371029,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787580627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189#discussion_r3844237338\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note: I think we could also save a lookup here by caching <code>CanonicalOptions</code> as well, but I didn't do it because that type has a bunch of fields and variants which I think would require either </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Making the C type messy and changing it whenever new canon opts are made. Or</li>\n<li>Boxing <code>CanonicalOptions</code> before storing it in <code>Func</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618371030,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787580627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton unassigned pchickey from <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189\">PR #14189 wasmtime: Cache <code>VMFuncRef</code> in <code>component::Func</code></a>.</p>",
        "id": 618385242,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787583988
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189#pullrequestreview-5009409069\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Nice wins! Do you have a relative breakdown of where the wins are coming from? For example which lookup is the most expensive?</p>\n<p>I'm a bit wary to inflate <code>component::Func</code> too too much to avoid duplicating information thoughout the runtime, so if some of the field movements are pretty minor in wins and one field predominantly dominates that might be a way to cut down on duplication. Naively for example I'd expect that <code>ExportIndex</code> would be relatively quick to lookup the type/options, and then the presence of post-return and async-ness in theory not too much more expensive when looking up the options themselves. Basically I'd expect that the <code>unsafe_func_ref</code> field to be the majority of the win here, but before actually changing anything here I'd want to confirm about where the performance wins come from</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618386018,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787584159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189#issuecomment-5397355921\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189\">PR #14189</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do you have a relative breakdown of where the wins are coming from? For example which lookup is the most expensive?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I didn't do a breakdown, but I can get one. Also I'm now realizing that <code>abi_info</code> gets called a few times, so maybe even if we don't include other fields in <code>Func</code> we can at least get some improvement by just calling <code>abi_info</code> once and reusing the result.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618388953,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787584788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189#issuecomment-5401282142\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14189\">PR #14189</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For the case of concurrency disabled, with just the <code>unsafe_func_ref</code> field I'm seeing a time of <code>180ns</code> (from the <code>300ns</code> original). So all the other fields together are an additional ~40ns. It's a bit hard to divide up the remaining amount between specific other fields because I'm seeing 10-20ns swings between runs anyway.</p>\n<p>I also realized we could mostly reuse the results of <code>abi_info</code> in the non-concurrent case without caching them in <code>Func</code> and that seems to give us most of the benefits anyway. With the existing changes I'm now seeing <code>140ns</code> with concurrency disabled (same as the original change) and <code>730ns</code> with concurrency enabled (not as big as the original change).</p>\n<p>I guess this means we could just use the <code>unsafe_func_ref</code> field and there's probably opportunity to improve the concurrent case as a follow up by reusing the results of <code>abi_info</code> more.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 618661336,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787605004
    },
